    "turn_text": "in what you just walked us through their congressman. So I just like to tease a little bit of it apart for our listeners and our viewers here. Let's talk a little bit about opposition research. As you said, this is something we're all intimately familiar with painfully. So what is opposition research? What do campaigns do? And what is the democratic congressional campaign committee's role? I keep using this big acronym that's going to wash over people. The D-Tree is the Democratic Party's the branch of the Democratic Party that focuses on US House races. You used to be in charge of it. So what do campaigns do and what does the DCCC do when it comes to opposition research?",
