    "turn_text": "Yeah, that's a great question. The mission of the DTC and the NRC and the DSCC and all of those acronyms, very simple, very simple. One mission, when, if you have one client as the chairman of the DCCC, just one, a democratic majority, And so you do everything you must do within the letter of the law in order to achieve that outcome. And sometimes it gets a little bit grisly and sometimes it doesn't look very pretty. But at the end of the day, your obligation is to make sure that the chair of the D triple that it is the Democrats who have the gavel so that they can enact an agenda that reflects the values and priorities of Democrats. And if you have a weak stomach and you're not willing to make those tough calls and do what needs to be done to get better candidates in the field, then you hold the wrong position within the",
