    "turn_text": "Well, this is interesting because I just received an hour before our conversation. copy of an invitation, Matt and Paul, that Santos has sent to his supporters. The invitation was discovered by Tuesday when I was paper. And in that invitation, he invites people to join him at his swearing in. but ask for a $100 and $250 donation. Now, that seems problematic to me. I'm not an ethics lawyer, but my understanding is, and I'm sure while you remember, you cannot use any official activity as a fundraiser. Anything that's happening. Now, many of our former colleagues would, of course, invite their supporters to the swearing-in. And they could, as I understand, use campaign proceeds to pay for a bus. But this is the first time I ever saw an invitation where somebody says, join me for my swearing-in $250 VIP, $100 supporter. And that gives you a sense of... I think every time we think we've gotten to the bottom of the story, it appears more bottomless. So we'll see where that goes. With respect to what the next few weeks hold, my guess, I think you're right. Paul, my guess is that Kevin McCarthy is trying to play out the clock on this. He needs Santos' vote on January 3rd because he doesn't have a very big margin. So he's got to have Santos' button to share, be or not, to vote for him. But then he's got a long-term challenge, and that is, If Santos decides to resign, or if he is forced out of his seat, the Republicans now have a special election in a Biden plus eight congressional district. That's going to cost them three, four, $5 million going to get national attention because of what Santos has done. And they're likely to lose a special in a Biden plus a district where you have a real candidate who's telling the truth. And that real, that's a severe problem for the Republican narrative. Just when you get the majority, you're down another one. And so my assumption would be that they will try and find a calculation that keeps this zombie well put Congressman Hodes keeps the zombie where he is and then toss him to the curb if he's not in federal prison by then, and then recruit another Republican to run in 24.",
