    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43479.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 88,
    "turn_text": "I used to call the people who drew those maps, Rembrandt and Picasos, on both sides of the aisle. I do believe, and I was outspoken on this, and it annoyed some of Paul's and my former colleagues, I do believe that the initial map in New York was overly aggressive. and that it was hard for a court, which was a Democratic court in New York, it was hard for them to justify it. It was just a little, I mean, my own district, which used to be fairly self-contained, sprawled across the Long Island Sound, it came very close to Paul Hoad's old district. Right? Right. That",
